PROCESS StandardTwoMergedIsNeverAnOutputReference
	SPEC "Every comparison of merge output is made against a reference output captured by the tool"
		+ "itself, never against the Standard-2 merged save of the input folder"
	REJECTED "Fixing the file to make it a reference: it would no longer have a known provenance"
	RATIONALE "The file was retouched and no version of the tool wrote it. Three of its four player"
		+ "identifiers are the rounded forms of real identifiers, but its host carries an"
		+ "identifier no number can produce through JSON serialization: at that magnitude only"
		+ "multiples of 16 are representable, and the two neighbouring doubles print as …60 and"
		+ "…70, while stringifyEntry has relied on that serialization since the first commit. The"
		+ "file also carries a byte order mark the tool never writes"
	SOURCE "Private context file known-issues/save-de-reference-standard-2-merged-retouchee.md, at"
		+ "tag pcst/before-awawa"
		REF @PROJECT.DNC
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-07"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

PROCESS AwawaAdoptionIsRevertibleByTagNotBranch
	SPEC "The state before awawa is marked by a tag in each of the three repositories:"
		+ "pcst/before-awawa in delairec/.do-not-commit, before-awawa in delairec/.ai, before-awawa"
		+ "on the task base of the public repository, the parent of the DEP2 merge"
	SPEC "No experimental branch exists: the three repositories keep their ordinary cycle, the"
		+ "private clone on planet-crafter-save-tools, the instructions by pull request on main,"
		+ "the public repository on its task base"
	REJECTED "Keeping a pcst/awawa branch and teaching install.sh an overridable branch: tooling"
		+ "added for a temporary effort"
	REJECTED "Naming the tag before-awawa in delairec/.do-not-commit, which carries several"
		+ "projects: the pcst/ prefix disambiguates it"
	RATIONALE "private:sync moves the private clone back to the branch named after the project,"
		+ "silently undoing an experimental branch there, whereas a tag depends on no current"
		+ "branch; the fallback needs no living branch, only a named point of return"
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-11, awawa installation session"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST61

PROCESS ATaskBranchIsRebasedNeverMerged
	SPEC "A task branch is updated by rebasing it on its base, never by merging the base into it"
	SPEC "Before working on an already pushed branch, and above all before handling a review, the"
		+ "base is checked to be an ancestor of HEAD; otherwise the branch is rebased and pushed"
		+ "with --force-with-lease before the first comment is read"
	REJECTED "Merging the base into the task branch"
	RATIONALE "The repository is a git machete stack, whose first traverse undoes a merge commit"
		+ "inside the stack; the base moves while a review is awaited, and reading the comments on"
		+ "a lagging branch means working on a state that no longer exists"
	SOURCE "private AGENTS.md, section Branches, at tag pcst/before-awawa"
		REF @PROJECT.DNC

PROCESS EveryWorktreeInstallsItsDependencies
	SPEC "bun install --frozen-lockfile runs in the worktree before the first test"
	SPEC "The branch of a new worktree is checked to start from the base in force"
	SPEC "input/ is linked from the main checkout when a task needs the reference saves, and the"
		+ "link is never staged"
	REJECTED "Relying on the node_modules of the main checkout"
	RATIONALE "Without its own install, Bun resolves the workspace packages through the"
		+ "node_modules of the main checkout: the tests run on the sources of another branch and"
		+ "pass silently, the costliest trap because it gives a verdict, and the wrong one; input/"
		+ "is not versioned, and a gitignore rule written for a directory lets the link escape and"
		+ "be staged by a global add"
	SOURCE "private AGENTS.md, section on working in a linked worktree, at tag pcst/before-awawa"
		REF @PROJECT.DNC

PROCESS AFixtureMayRestOnAKnownDefect
	SPEC "A fixture may rest on a known defect, provided the LIMITATION of that defect names the"
		+ "spec to rewrite once it is fixed"
	SPEC "The coupling is documented on the side of the defect, never on the side of the test"
	REJECTED "Fabricating an input that never occurs to avoid depending on a defect"
	REJECTED "Documenting the coupling on the side of the test"
	RATIONALE "Some behaviours have no natural producer, since checking that an invalid output is"
		+ "reported needs an input that produces one, and the only honest arrangement is then a"
		+ "real defect rather than a fabricated input never met; the limitation is what is read"
		+ "when the defect is fixed, and it carries the proof that the spec fails once the defect"
		+ "is gone and what to do then: find another producer, not merely turn the assertion green"
		+ "again"
	SOURCE "private AGENTS.md, at tag pcst/before-awawa"
		REF @PROJECT.DNC
	SOURCE "example in force since PR #59"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST59

PROCESS EverythingLandsInTheTaskPullRequest
	SPEC "A task pull request carries no To do at merge comment: what that checklist inventoried"
		+ "enters the corpus when the decision is taken, not at the merge"
	SPEC "The corpus changes a task delivers are made in the task pull request itself, pushed once"
		+ "it is opened and its number known, before its review, and the review checks them against"
		+ "the diff as it checks the code"
	SPEC "The corpus holds only tasks delivered in this repository; work on another project is"
		+ "archived with a DESC saying so, and carried out outside this procedure"
	SPEC "Nothing is recorded after the merge: whether a rule belongs to the general instructions"
		+ "or to the project is settled during the review, through /awawa-pr-review, before the"
		+ "pull request is flagged ready"
	SPEC "The usage report is committed on the task branch once the review is addressed, and after"
		+ "the merge only the worktrees are cleaned"
	REJECTED "Recording after the merge in a follow-up pull request: one more pull request per"
		+ "round, with nothing to record from the second one on"
	REJECTED "A single /awawa-pr-review command covering both moments"
	REJECTED "A task naming another project by APPLIES_TO_PROJECT, promoted in a companion pull"
		+ "request: its IMPL anchors resolve against this workspace only, so lint refuses the"
		+ "promotion (L016), or accepts a path that names a file of this repository instead"
	REJECTED "Promoting a task delivered in another repository after the merge of its delivery pull"
		+ "request: the tasks must stay true to what was delivered"
	REJECTED "Keeping the checklist emptied of what the corpus carries: what is left is not worth"
		+ "the discipline it costs"
	REJECTED "Keeping a pull request comment for the residue meant for ~/.ai alone: an entity"
		+ "carries it better, typed, queryable and visible at every status"
	REJECTED "Fixing /pr-merge-followup and /pr-review-followup in place: they serve the projects"
		+ "without a corpus and keep their form"
	RATIONALE "The checklist existed because an inventory disappears with the session of the task"
		+ "agent; the corpus is that inventory and does not disappear, and since it lives in the"
		+ "branch, a change made there travels with the pull request; every post-merge pass opened"
		+ "one more pull request, as PR #65 led to PR #66 and PR #68 to PR #69"
		REF @DECISION.TheCorpusLivesInThePublicRepository
		REF @DECISION.AUsageReportIsCommittedInTheTaskPullRequest
	SOURCE "decision of 2026-09-11, awawa installation session"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST70
	SOURCE "user ruling of 2026-09-13 on PR #69, delivered by PR #70"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST69
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST70

PROCESS AnImplAnchorNamesAFileOrASymbol
	SPEC "An IMPL anchor under a SPEC names a file or a symbol, and a directory only for an"
		+ "obligation that covers a whole layer, which the SPEC then says"
	REJECTED "A shape on anchors: the binary only knows the anchor term, and a shape refuses"
		+ "references and does not apply to that term"
	REJECTED "Rewriting the existing directory anchors at once: most carry layer obligations,"
		+ "written as such"
	RATIONALE "A discipline, not a schema rule: an anchor is path[:line][::literal] with no shape"
		+ "applying to it, and L016 resolves a directory, so a directory anchor never fails;"
		+ "enforcing it awaits an option of the tool, and an obligation of absence has no literal"
		+ "to anchor anyway"
	SOURCE "PR #68 merged, user ruling of 2026-09-13 on PR #69"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST68
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST69

PROCESS TheCorpusHoldsNoViewItAlreadyRenders
	SPEC "Nothing the corpus already renders is written in it: no dependency graph in a comment,"
		+ "the AFTER edges carrying it"
	SPEC "A task split is not recorded as a decision: the TASK entities it produces carry it, and"
		+ "why a SPEC line lands on a given deliverable is written in the RATIONALE of that"
		+ "deliverable"
	REJECTED "Keeping an ASCII graph of the task dependencies: no command reads it, and status,"
		+ "refs and context render the same edges"
	REJECTED "A DECISION per task split: it copies the DESC of the entities produced and restates"
		+ "alternatives the general rule already rejects"
	RATIONALE "The ASCII graph heading the task file was edited by hand at every split since it was"
		+ "written: derived information the tool manual forbids keeping elsewhere, wrong at the"
		+ "next commit and read by no command; the split decision of the UI test harness held,"
		+ "beyond the descriptions of its tasks, only alternatives the general rule had already"
		+ "rejected, and its removal lost no sentence"
	SOURCE "review of PR #75, user ruling of 2026-09-14"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST75

PROCESS ATestTaskChangesTheUiOnlyForItsOwnSake
	REJECTED "Changing the interface for the sole convenience of a locator"
	SPEC "An unrequested interface change is acceptable in a test task only if it is worth having"
		+ "on its own, outside the test"
	RATIONALE "A file input without a label stays reachable by its role and accessible name, so no"
		+ "test rule requires changing the interface to make a field reachable; the change under"
		+ "review was kept only once its own reason, an accessibility gain, was stated"
	SOURCE "Review of T23"
		REF @PULL_REQUEST.PCST38

PROCESS AnEntityThatStopsBindingIsArchivedByThePullRequestThatEndsIt
	SPEC "An entity that stops binding is archived in the pull request that ends it: STATUS"
		+ "archived and ARCHIVED_ON that day, never deleted there"
	SPEC "A ruling replaced on the same subject is rewritten in place under its name, the previous"
		+ "form becoming a REJECTED line when it teaches something"
	REJECTED "Keeping history in the corpus with superseded entities, SUPERSEDES and CLOSES edges"
		+ "and :v2 successors: every context loaded the dead entities, and the edges had to be"
		+ "maintained by hand"
	REJECTED "Deleting an entity the day it stops binding: the references to it break in the same"
		+ "pull request, and nothing lists what was removed"
	RATIONALE "Measured before the migration of 2026-09-17: 47 STATUS superseded, 26 SUPERSEDES, 34"
		+ "CLOSES and 44 :v2 written by hand, and 41 closed questions and 12 superseded decisions"
		+ "loaded by context; an archived entity is suppressed by the schema gate, named in the"
		+ "context footer and deleted by the cleanup pass once its delay has run"

PROCESS WhatShouldNeverHaveBeenRecordedIsDeletedAtOnce
	SPEC "An entity that should never have been recorded is deleted by hand at once, with every"
		+ "reference line to it, instead of being archived"
	REJECTED "Archiving it like an entity that once bound: it would stay in the corpus for the"
		+ "whole delay, and its archive would say it once held"
	RATIONALE "Archiving is for what stopped binding; an entity under the recording threshold never"
		+ "bound anything"
		REF @PROCESS.ADecisionIsRecordedOnlyIfAPullRequestCouldReverseIt

PROCESS ADecisionIsRecordedOnlyIfAPullRequestCouldReverseIt
	SPEC "A DECISION or a PROCESS is recorded only if a future pull request could do the reverse by"
		+ "mistake"
	SPEC "A rule that is general to every project is recorded in the general instructions, never in"
		+ "this corpus"
	REJECTED "Recording every ruling a review or a session produces: the sessions of 2026-09-11 to"
		+ "2026-09-16 ran awawa new DECISION 13 times and awawa new OPEN_QUESTION 11 times for 10"
		+ "tasks, and the user judged there were too many decisions they would not have recorded"
	RATIONALE "The threshold of an OPEN_QUESTION is held by the schema, BLOCKS @TASK being"
		+ "required; the threshold of a ruling cannot be, so it is a conduct rule read by the"
		+ "review"
